To run this simulation, execute the script ```runall```.

This simulation requires sumo-launchd to be running.

This test checks if fullDuplex communication between a SatCar and a LEO satellite works if it is enabled and does not work if it is disabled.
There are four test cases:
 0: fullDuplex enabled, SatCar receives transmission from LEO while the SatCar sends --> both packets received
 1: fullDuplex enabled, LEO receives transmission from SatCar while the LEO sends --> both packets received
 2: fullDuplex disabled, SatCar receives transmission from LEO while the SatCar sends --> only LEO receives a packet, as the SatCar's reception is interfered by LEO transmission
 3: fullDuplex disabled, LEO receives transmission from SatCar while the LEO sends --> only SatCar receives a packet, as the LEO's reception is interfered by the SatCar transmission

To compensate for the long propagation delay between SatCar and LEO satellite different start times of the application are configured for the SatCar and the LEO satellite, respectively.

If full duplex communication is enabled, all packets ever transmitted should be received.
If full duplex communication is disabled, only the second of the two configured packet transmission should be successful as only the first one is interfered by the second transmission.
